# TRMNL Framework 3.4

Reference: [Framework 3.4 docs](https://trmnl.com/framework/docs/3.4) · [Upgrade guide](https://trmnl.com/framework/docs/3.4/v3_upgrade_guide) · [UI Framework versioning](https://help.trmnl.com/en/articles/14135346-ui-framework-versioning)

Plugins pin a release with `framework_version: "3.4.0"` in `settings.yml`. Leave that as a specific version. `latest` follows every new Framework CSS release.

## Where to look

- **Guides**: V3.4 Overview, Upgrade, Enhancement, TRMNL X.
- **Utilities**: Size, Spacing, Gap, Flex, Grid, Background, Border, Rounded, Outline, Visibility, Responsive, Text, Image, Scale, Aspect Ratio.
- **Runtime**: Overflow, Clamp, Format Value, Fit Value, Content Limiter, Pixel Perfect, Framework Runtime.
- **Foundation**: Screen, View, Layout, Title Bar, Columns, Mashup.
- **Elements**: Title, Value, Label, Description, Divider.
- **Components**: Rich Text, Item, Table, Chart, Progress.

## Conventions

- Use Framework 3.4 utilities and components. Size classes use a double hyphen: `w--full`, `h--28`.
- Horizontal rules use shade steps `border--h-10` through `border--h-75`, plus `border--h-black` and `border--h-white`.
- Muted copy uses `text--muted`. The old `label--muted` and `b-h-gray-*` classes are absent from the 3.4 stylesheet.
- v2 and v3 class names still render. New features (themes, paint API, adaptive charts and icons) are opt-in.
